      "beat_id": "B05TIMING",
      "act": "SHOW",
      "heading": "Exploratory timing diagnostic",
      "narration_text": "Fixing it taught me something about measurement. In an exploratory check at level two, the middle difficulty, I compared the deadline-first strategy using fresh information with the same strategy checking for updates less often, across twenty matched pairs of worlds. In the original schedule, every batch of requests arrived on a round when the slower check ran, so checking less often cost nothing: the average gap was zero. When I shifted that check one round later, the average coverage gap was twenty-two point nine percentage points. The shifted schedule also made one extra status check per shift.",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "bm_fable",
      "t_start": 75.708,
      "estimated_duration_s": 37.8,
